ALBUKHR Testnet U2A Acceptance Test Plan
Prerequisite: Use a disposable Testnet Supabase branch and isolated Testnet app/API deployment. Keep TESTNET_U2A_INVESTMENT_ENABLED=false until environment checks and source review are complete. Use only Pi Testnet amounts. Never run these cases against Mainnet.
A. Project and term eligibility
network=testnet, project status approved, allowed type (core, internal, external), and one active term: the terms endpoint returns only that project's active term(s).
Same project with status active: terms may be returned and test investment may be started.
Project with draft, rejected, suspended, or any other unsupported status: terms endpoint and payment approval fail before Pi approval.
Project ID and project code that do not belong to the same row: reject.
A Mainnet project ID, Mainnet-only project, or network=mainnet metadata: reject; no Mainnet Supabase request or write is allowed.
Unknown project type: reject.
No term, inactive term, invalid duration, duplicate active terms for one duration, invalid min stake, or invalid reward rate: reject/keep UI locked.
Amount below the exact selected term's minimum: reject before payment; server rechecks it after PaymentDTO retrieval.
Amount equal to or above minimum: continue only if all server-side checks pass; do not invent a max-stake limit absent from the current Testnet terms schema.
B. PaymentDTO and identity validation
Missing/expired/revoked Testnet session on terms or approve/complete: reject.
Missing or invalid Pi access token, or Pi /me returns no UID: reject.
PaymentDTO network not Pi Testnet/testnet: reject.
direction other than user_to_app: reject.
Missing or mismatched user_uid against Pi /me: reject.
Missing configured Testnet App wallet: gateway must fail at initialization and remain disabled.
Missing to_address or destination not equal to the configured Testnet App wallet: reject before approval and settlement.
Payment identifier absent, or PaymentDTO identifier differs from requested ID: reject.
Metadata action/network/project ID/project code/duration/term ID mismatch: reject.
Missing matching Testnet public.users row for the verified Pi UID: reject closed; do not provision a user within the settlement RPC.
Pi payment cancelled: reject and create no stake.
C. Two-phase payment lifecycle
Valid pending payment: server inserts one pending investment intent including immutable term snapshot before attempting Pi approval.
Pi approval request fails: do not create a stake; verify intent remains retryable and no liquidity record is created.
Pi approval succeeds: reread PaymentDTO from Pi, verify it, and mark the intent approved.
Client claims success but Pi API says not completed: reject and create no stake.
Pi reports developer completion but transaction not verified (status.transaction_verified and transaction.verified are false): reject and create no stake.
Transaction ID missing or mismatched: reject.
Pi completion succeeds and transaction is verified: exactly one verified payment intent and one Testnet stake are committed atomically.
Repeat /complete with the same completed payment ID: return the original stake idempotently; do not insert a second stake or double-count funds.
Call /incomplete without a pre-existing investment intent: reject; do not settle an arbitrary payment from client-supplied metadata.
Incomplete callback for an existing approved payment: reload PaymentDTO server-to-server, verify it, complete if appropriate, then settle once.
Reuse a known payment ID with different user, amount, project, term, duration, or recipient: reject.
Simulate concurrent completion callbacks for the same ID: only one stake/payment settlement exists; other callback returns idempotently or a safe retryable conflict.
Database/RPC timeout after Pi completion: retry must reconcile the same payment and not create duplicate stakes.
D. Ledger, rewards, and withdrawals
New Testnet stake references investment_payment_id; payment_record_id remains NULL for that new U2A stake.
New stake must not insert into or increment project_liquidity_payments.
Existing liquidity records and existing stakes' payment_record_id references are unchanged by the migration.
New stakes preserve the selected Testnet term snapshot: term ID, duration, minimum, reward rate, formula, project/network, and capture time.
Using the reviewed reward formula, calculate rewards from at least two known amounts and compare with approved expected results. Do not enable if formula semantics disagree.
Stake appears only in public.stakes with network='testnet', the correct Testnet user, and unlock_at = start_at + duration_days.
Existing Testnet investor data query returns the new stake for the matching Testnet Pi UID and returns no stake to a different UID.
Testnet withdrawal endpoints can read the new stake, verify identity, calculate eligibility/fees, and apply existing unlock logic. Do not request a real payout as part of this integration test until payout test procedures are approved.
Verify no Mainnet table/endpoint is called or modified at any point.
E. Feature flag / operational controls
Feature flag unset, empty, false, or any non-true value: API does not mount the new routes; /testnet-investment/terms returns 404.
Feature flag true but App wallet absent or Pi API key absent: process refuses to start rather than enabling an unverified gateway.
Feature flag true in explicitly isolated Testnet deployment with verified Testnet configuration: only the new /testnet-investment routes become reachable.
Existing /liquidity-payment/*, withdrawal, admin, and payout flows pass their prior regression tests without behavior changes.
Cache busting/versioning causes browsers to load the new client only after the app assets are deployed to Testnet.
User-facing copy states TESTNET and makes clear this is testing only/no Mainnet investment value.
Pass criteria
All applicable cases pass in disposable Testnet integration. Zero duplicate stakes; zero writes to liquidity-payment ledger for an investment payment; zero Mainnet accesses/writes; correct RPC grants (service_role only); existing liquidity/withdrawal regressions remain green. Store sanitized test identifiers and results—never store API keys, access tokens, session tokens, or private keys.
